  "name": "fills_gradient",
  "description": "The shared Fill type on all four keys that carry one: a shape's body, a gauge's track, the area under a chart, and the shape's background. Pins the three decisions the two implementations could disagree about. A fill beats the flat colour beside it, and the flat colour is still written as the gradient's first stop so an older app draws something sensible. A rule that recolours a layer drops its gradient, and so does a gauge's colour table, because both say something about this reading and a gradient does not. A gradient on a bars chart is not an area fill and resolves to nothing.",
